		<member name="override_log_level" type="bool" setter="set_override_log_level" getter="get_override_log_level" default="false">
			When [code]false[/code] the [code]chorus/logging/min_level[/code] project setting decides how much this node hears. Turn it on to let [member log_level] override the project for this node alone.
		</member>
		<member name="log_level" type="int" setter="set_log_level" getter="get_log_level" default="2">
			The least severe [enum LogLevelCode] worth reporting; anything below it is never built. [constant LOG_OFF] silences the node entirely. Only consulted when [member override_log_level] is on. The level travels with the engine's configuration, so a change takes effect at the next [method load_model].
		</member>
